# WP-FAR-12D (11-22): far crowd figures keep a minimum screen size. A VAT (far LOD) figure whose true projected
# size (FOV-aware, LODDistanceScale removed) is below VertexAnimationCrowd::kMinScreenSize (0.012 of the view
# height) is drawn grown about its feet to that size, capped at x6; near / skeletal figures unchanged.
# Readout: editor.log "[Crowd] skeletal N, vat M, draws D, grown to min screen size G (max xS)".
# Scene: CesiumMan at the origin + 20 copies spread 30-300 m behind it (WP_FAR11_SkinnedCrowd).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_FAR11_SkinnedCrowd.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Когда run Mode "Select mode"
Когда run Action "Play from Here"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 90
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,6000
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,0,-1
Когда advance 2
Тогда high_60 at 60 m under High the origin figure is unchanged vs dev (its own size); the far figures are no smaller than before
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,30000
Когда advance 2
Тогда high_300 at 300 m under High the crowd (300-600 m away) reads as walking figures, not dots; log: [Crowd] grown G > 0, max scale <= 6
Когда run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance Cinematic"
Когда advance 2
Тогда cine_300 the same 300 m view under Cinematic: the crowd reads as walking figures, not dots; log: [Crowd] grown G > 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,6000
Когда advance 2
Тогда cine_60 at 60 m under Cinematic the origin figure is walking, its own size
Когда run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,3000
Когда advance 2
Тогда high_30 control: at 30 m under High the origin figure is unchanged vs dev
# WP-FAR-10E / WP-FAR-10F (proof added by WP-PROOF-1126): a follower mesh (ModularCharacter attachFollowerMesh -
# Animation::LeaderPoseLink, a runtime component, so it is attached in Play) takes its leader's frame in
# MeshRenderer::SelectSkinnedLods: the leader's LOD clamped to its own levels, the leader's VAT hand-off (same clip,
# same time) and the leader's MinScreenScale about the leader's feet. The follower here is a second CesiumMan.skmesh
# on the origin figure 'CesiumMan', so a correct follower lies exactly on its leader (one figure, never two).
# Readout: editor.log "[SkinnedLOD] entity F: LOD l/n skins ... influences, the level of its leader L[ (vertex
# animation)]" (F = the follower, L = CesiumMan's entity) - a follower line never states "screen size".
Когда lua "local f = World.find('CesiumMan'):attachFollowerMesh('Meshes/Displace/CesiumMan.skmesh'); assert(f ~= nil, 'attachFollowerMesh returned nothing'); print(string.format('WP-PROOF follower id %s', tostring(f)))"
Когда advance 2
Тогда follower_30 WP-FAR-10F at 30 m under High: one walking origin figure, the follower exactly on it (no second figure, no offset, no z-fight flicker); log: "[SkinnedLOD] entity F: LOD l/n ... the level of its leader L" with l = the leader's own LOD in its last "[SkinnedLOD] entity L" line
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,0,30000
Когда advance 2
Тогда follower_300 WP-FAR-10E + 10F at 300 m under High: the origin figure is grown to the min screen size (as high_300) and the follower is grown with it - same size, same feet, no small figure inside or beside a big one; log: the follower's line "LOD n/n ... the level of its leader L (vertex animation)" (the leader's coarsest level, VAT), "[Crowd] ... grown to min screen size G" with G counting the follower too (G = high_300's G + 1)
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 10
Когда advance 2
Тогда follower_zoom WP-FAR-10F FOV 10 at 300 m: leader and follower large and skeletal again, together; log: the follower's new line without "(vertex animation)", its LOD = the leader's new LOD
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 90
Когда run Action "Stop"
